# Controlled Validation

Source:

```text
WIN11-01
10.10.10.101
```

Target:

```text
WIN11-02
10.10.10.102
```

Account:

```text
CORP\tadmin
```

Connection:

```cmd
net use \\10.10.10.102\C$ /user:CORP\tadmin *
```

Administrative-share access:

```cmd
dir \\10.10.10.102\C$
```

This safely generated the remote administrative authentication behavior required by DET-006.

---

# Positive Validation

A fresh SMB connection was established from WIN11-01 to WIN11-02.

The resulting Windows Security Event 4624 was identified with:

```text
Logon Type 3
Source: 10.10.10.101
Account: tadmin
Target: WIN11-02
```

DET-006 identified the event.

Result:

```text
DET-006 TRIGGERED
```

**Positive Test:** PASS

---

# Negative Validation

A local successful authentication event was generated without remote SMB access.

Because it was not the validated privileged network-logon pattern, DET-006 did not trigger.

Result:

```text
DET-006 NOT TRIGGERED
```

**Negative Test:** PASS

